It's easy to add such a phrase to the email body of the contact form with a small 3rd plugin. I didn't think too much about it but something like this should work:
```
 public function onSubmitContact(&$contact, &$data)
 {
  if (JPluginHelper::isEnabled('content', 'confirmconsent'))
  {
   if (isset($data['consentbox']) && !empty($data['consentbox']))
   {
    $data['contact_message'] .= "\n\n" . 'The user accepted the privacy policy to process this request on DATE';
   }
   // Nearly impossible(?):
   else
   {
    // Say this 
   }
  }
  else
  {
   // Say that
  }
  return true;
 }
```
